# netsurf: tap a text field to type; stale focus crash; document.compareDocumentPosition; ordered script-inserted scripts; SVG aspect ratio
#
# Hardware run 20 (Google sign-in in the claude.ai popup) and its replay:
#
# - vita: a tap or CROSS click that lands in a text field opens the keyboard
#   (browser_window_get_features says CTX_FORM_TEXT under the point), as on
#   a phone. The field showed "Click to edit this field" and the user tapped
#   it again and again: nothing said TRIANGLE opens the keyboard. Off while
#   the autotest drives the controls.
# - html_keypress: the focus owner is a raw box pointer that a script-driven
#   relayout frees; the next key was dispatched to freed memory (simulator
#   SIGSEGV after Google replaced its form). A focused box no longer in the
#   tree loses the focus.
# - polyfill: document.compareDocumentPosition / document.contains (elements
#   had them). Google's "is it in the page" test threw there, failing its
#   viewport service and every service behind it, the Next button's among
#   them ("Failed to retrieve dependencies of service ...": 137 -> 0).
# - script-inserted scripts without an async attribute run in insertion
#   order (HTML's async = false list; the bridge cannot tell set-false from
#   untouched): Google's loader inserts dependent bundles back to back and a
#   small one ran before the big one it calls into ("not a function").
# - inline <svg>: scaled per its viewBox to fit and centred
#   (preserveAspectRatio's default) instead of stretched to the box.
#
# Still open: Google's sign-in "Next" -- the click reaches Google's event
# contract on <html> (trusted, button 0) with the email in the field, and
# its modules now load without errors, but no request is sent (doc 12).
